From ceae6729a8f0b33d0434c88f3753b195c58086ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Hwan Kim <karmaddee@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:34:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: take the host's application icon before reading the
 exe's.

set_app_icon read the exe's icon resource first and only then looked at
WINE_APP_ICON_PATH. For some programs that read never comes back to
set_app_icon: with Mecharashi (Unity), NtUserDrawIconEx reports "Error
retrieving icon frame 0" while the icon images are made and nothing after
create_app_icon_images() runs in that process, although the thread goes on
to create its windows. Neither the exe's icon nor the host's then reaches
the Dock, and the application stays on the generic executable icon.

Look at the host's icon first and read the exe's resource only when the
host named none. A launcher that passes WINE_APP_ICON_PATH gets its icon
whatever the exe's resource does.

This does not fix the read itself: a program started without
WINE_APP_ICON_PATH still loses its icon when the read fails.
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/window.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
index 55cec6f..bff2443 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -841,7 +841,7 @@ static BOOL running_image_is(const char *exe_name)
 
 static void set_app_icon(void)
 {
-    CFArrayRef images = create_app_icon_images();
+    CFArrayRef images = NULL;
     CFURLRef icon_url = NULL;
     const char *icon_path, *owner;
 
@@ -856,6 +856,13 @@ static void set_app_icon(void)
                                                            strlen(icon_path), FALSE);
     }
 
+    /* The exe's resource is only read when the host named no icon. Reading it
+     * can fail in a way that never comes back here (seen with a Unity game:
+     * NtUserDrawIconEx cannot retrieve a frame, and the rest of this function
+     * does not run), which left the application on the generic icon even with
+     * an icon from the host. */
+    if (!icon_url) images = create_app_icon_images();
+
     if (images || icon_url)
     {
         macdrv_set_application_icon(images, icon_url);
